  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Target answers are only set-2 simple past: took, gave, wrote, spoke, broke, flew, grew, drew, blew, drank, drove, rode, sang, began, fell, found, heard, told, wore, woke, won, hid, left, kept, felt, built, chose, froze, stood, dug, hung, knew, threw.",
      "Never target set-1 past: went, saw, ate, came, ran, sat, got, made, was, had, did, said. Those may be wrong choices only.",
      "Each item has four unique one-word choices: the matching simple past, the present base, an -ed overregularization, and a participle or a different irregular past.",
      "Only one choice can fit a yesterday reading of the stem. Participles like given, begun, broken, taken, and hidden are wrong unless the stem has have or has, which it must not.",
      "Stems stay in kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands. No real names. Use <NAME> when a person is named.",
      "Keep overregularizations kid-like and pronounceable, such as drawed, gived, or beginned. Do not use hanged for hang."
    ]
  },
